      "from": "editions/scrapedo.env.example",
      "diff": "--- core/.env.example\n+++ scrapedo/.env.example\n@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@\n-# walmart-azure-headless: environment for a local run (copy to .env, never commit .env).\n+# walmart-azure-headless, Scrape.do edition: environment for a local run (copy to .env, never commit .env).\n+# The edition runs Scrape.do only (docs/EDITIONS.md): it needs no Oxylabs key and refuses an Oxylabs run.\n # In Azure these are set on the job; the secrets are Key Vault references (see docs/AZURE.md).\n \n-# PostgreSQL (psycopg). A password may be in the URL or in PGPASSWORD.\n-WALMART_COLLECTOR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://walmart_collector@localhost:5432/walmart_collector\n+# PostgreSQL (psycopg): a database of this edition's own, never the other edition's. A password may be in the\n+# URL or in PGPASSWORD.\n+WALMART_COLLECTOR_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://walmart_collector@localhost:5432/walmart_scrapedo\n # PGPASSWORD=\n # entra = Azure Database for PostgreSQL with the job's managed identity (no password)\n # WALMART_COLLECTOR_DATABASE_AUTH=entra\n@@ -11,15 +13,10 @@\n SCRAPEDO_API_KEY=\n # SCRAPEDO_API_KEY_FILE=/mnt/secrets/scrapedo-api-key\n \n-# Oxylabs Web API, for a store whose provider is oxylabs: its Bearer key itself, or a file holding it. Not\n-# credentials of the Oxylabs Classic product. Each edition (editions/) names its own provider's key only.\n-# OXYLABS_WEB_API_KEY=\n-# OXYLABS_WEB_API_KEY_FILE=/mnt/secrets/oxylabs-web-api-key\n-\n-# Configuration and storage\n+# Configuration and storage: a data folder (or blob container) of this edition's own\n WALMART_COLLECTOR_CONFIG=config/collector.yaml\n+WALMART_COLLECTOR_DATA_DIR=./data\n # WALMART_COLLECTOR_STORAGE=azure_blob\n # WALMART_COLLECTOR_BLOB_ACCOUNT_URL=https://<account>.blob.core.windows.net\n-# WALMART_COLLECTOR_BLOB_CONTAINER=walmart-collector\n-# WALMART_COLLECTOR_DATA_DIR=./data\n+# WALMART_COLLECTOR_BLOB_CONTAINER=walmart-collector-scrapedo\n # WALMART_COLLECTOR_LOG_LEVEL=INFO\n"
    },
    {
